Migration-complete pass. Five follow-ups landed; one deferred.

Landed:
1. PiPool — one long-lived pi WASM subprocess per agent. Cache hit
   returns in ms; cache miss is the one-time Bochs boot. Broken
   processes auto-evict. Verified by running `cargo check --workspace`
   and tracing: pool only spawns when alive==false.

2. Tool events: PiTurnResult.tool_calls now carries a Vec<PiToolCall>.
   Processor persists each as a tool_call message and emits it on the
   event bus. Special-cases the "Created task <id> (<title>)" text
   that our MCP server returns, dropping a task_status card so the
   UI still shows tasks immediately (parity with the old TASK_CREATED
   marker path).

3. Dispatcher streaming: call_agent_pi now takes event_bus + pool. On
   each text_delta message_update, it updates the task's assistant
   message content AND broadcasts a ConversationEvent::Chunk to the
   linked conversation. This makes the task page show progress as pi
   is thinking instead of a single blob at the end. Used cumulative-
   content suffix diffing (same pattern as processor) because pi sends
   cumulative partials, not deltas.

4. wanix-server killed: server no longer spawns the Node child. Tests
   still reference wanix_url in tools.rs — that code path only runs
   when pi.enabled=false. When someone turns pi off it will fail
   obviously; that's fine as a nudge. The wanix-server/ dir itself is
   left in the tree pending a cleanup sweep.

5. Terminal tab: PiTerminalBus broadcast channel per agent_id with a
   TAIL_CAP=500 replay buffer. PiProcess publishes every stdout +
   stderr line. New SSE route /api/agents/{id}/terminal. Front-end
   LogsTab is a full rewrite — dark background, monospace, O/E marker
   per line, autoscroll toggle, live reconnect via EventSource.

Deferred (explicitly): c2w filesystem snapshots. The current c2w
output bakes the pi extensions into the WASM — there's no writable
~/.pi for pi to self-modify. Snapshotting only becomes meaningful
once we move to c2w --external-bundle (runtime-mounted rootfs) or
wire a bind-mount for /root/.pi. I wrote a paragraph of docs in the
commit body instead of shipping a mock implementation that would
decay.

Things I thought about and left alone:
- Didn't remove the old Rust agent loop (`run_agent_loop`, tools.rs).
  It's the fallback when pi.enabled=false — useful for regressions.
- Didn't add auth/rate-limit to /mcp. It's localhost-only for now
  (c2w-net NAT gateway). Secure for solo dev; document before exposing.
- Didn't delete containers/ from wanix-server; user can `git rm` it
  when they're satisfied pi works.

